#question(title: [Functions, inverses, and graphs - 2])[
  Draw the graph of a function $f$ satisfying
  all of the following:

  + The domain of $f$ is $RR$.
  + $f$ is differentiable everywhere.
  + The restriction of $f$ to
    $display([0 comma oo))$ is one-to-one,  \
     and its INVERSE has a vertical tangent
     line at $2$.
  + The restriction of $f$ to
    $display((- oo comma 0])$ is one-to-one,
     \
     and its INVERSE has derivative $2$ at
     $2$.
]
